// A bandit shakedown - the example conversation, in Yarn. Written for the Ink-vs-Yarn spike and
// kept for dialog Slice 3 to put on a Bandit in game.
//
// gold() is a question the game answers. <<TakeMoney>> and <<ChangeStanding>> are actions the game
// carries out (Raiders is the Bandit's faction id). $asked_about_road is Yarn's own memory, local
// to this conversation. Each #line: tag is the line's id - what crosses the network, what a
// translation keys on, and what a voice recording would be filed under.
//
// Compile with: ysc compile shakedown.yarn -o . -n shakedown
// which writes shakedown.yarnc (the program) and shakedown-Lines.csv (every line's text by id).

title: Shakedown
---
<<declare $asked_about_road = false>>
Bandit: Toll road. Twenty gold, or you walk back the way you came. #line:shakedown_toll
<<jump Choices>>
===

title: Choices
---
-> Pay the toll. <<if gold() >= 20>> #line:shakedown_pay
    <<TakeMoney 20>>
    Bandit: Pleasure doing business. Road's yours. #line:shakedown_paid
-> Who says it's your road? <<if not $asked_about_road>> #line:shakedown_ask
    <<set $asked_about_road to true>>
    Bandit: The twelve of us in those rocks say so. #line:shakedown_twelve
    <<jump Choices>>
-> Get out of my way. #line:shakedown_refuse
    <<ChangeStanding Raiders -10>>
    Bandit: Wrong answer. #line:shakedown_wrong
===
